From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson: hdmi: balance mode_config suspend/resume across HPD events

Fixes found by the S905X5/CoreELEC driver review:

- F014 drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c:2591: HPD callback's drm_mode_config_helper_suspend/resume are unbalanced: repeated plugout leaks the saved atomic state; the resume paths skip the cb and leave DRM suspended

See the review diary (S905X5-DRIVER-REVIEW-DIARY.md) for the defect
analysis and the forum discussion.

final judge sign-off did not run, so this patch still needs a human
read before it is proposed upstream. Not yet exercised on S905X5 hardware.

diff --git a/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c b/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
index 71b7e66..514444d 100644

--- a/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/meson_hdmi.c
@@ -2621,14 +2621,26 @@ static void meson_hdmitx_hpd_cb(void *data)
 		cec_notifier_set_phys_addr_from_edid(am_hdmi->cec_notifier,
 						     pedid);
 		kfree(pedid);
-		if (mode_config.suspend_state)
-			drm_mode_config_helper_resume(drm);
 	} else {
 		DRM_DEBUG("%s[%d]\n", __func__, __LINE__);
 		cec_notifier_set_phys_addr(am_hdmi->cec_notifier,
 					   CEC_PHYS_ADDR_INVALID);
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The callback can fire several times for the same hpd level
+	 * (resume, fake_plug, spurious irq). Only this path uses
+	 * suspend_state, so use it to keep suspend and resume balanced: a
+	 * second suspend would overwrite and leak the saved state.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&meson_hdmitx_hpd_pm_lock);
+	if (hdmitx_get_hpd_state(tx_comm)) {
+		if (drm->mode_config.suspend_state)
+			drm_mode_config_helper_resume(drm);
+	} else if (!drm->mode_config.suspend_state) {
 		drm_mode_config_helper_suspend(drm);
 	}
+	mutex_unlock(&meson_hdmitx_hpd_pm_lock);
 #endif
 
 	edid_raw_len = hdmitx_common_read_edid(&edid_raw_buf);
